upsc.append({"q":"Which one of the following statements about the functional classification of towns, per Goh Cheng Leong, is NOT correct?","o":["An entrepôt port, such as Singapore, Colombo or Rotterdam, is one that primarily receives goods for its own domestic consumption and rarely redistributes them elsewhere","Ecclesiastical towns, such as Jerusalem, Mecca and Varanasi, are historical and religious centres frequented by pilgrims worldwide","Mining towns like Kalgoorlie (gold), Sudbury (nickel) and Potosi (tin) may shrink once minerals are exhausted, though some acquire other functions and persist","Administrative towns are the headquarters of government, such as Washington D.C., Canberra and Brasilia"],"a":0,"e":"This statement is incorrect and reverses the actual definition — an entrepôt port is explicitly defined as one that RECEIVES AND REDISTRIBUTES goods to neighbouring countries and around the world, not one focused on domestic consumption. The other three statements are correct."})

