upsc.append({"q":"Consider the following statements about the evolution of Indian towns, per NCERT — entirely new content not found in Goh Cheng Leong:\n1. NCERT classifies Indian towns by era into Ancient, Medieval and Modern towns.\n2. Ancient towns like Varanasi, Prayag (Allahabad), Pataliputra (Patna) and Madurai mostly developed as religious and cultural centres.\n3. All of India's medieval fort-towns, such as Delhi, Jaipur and Agra, were built on entirely new sites with no connection to earlier ancient settlements.\nWhich of the statements given above is/are correct?","o":["1 and 2 only","1 and 3 only","2 and 3 only","1, 2 and 3"],"a":0,"e":"Statement 3 is incorrect — NCERT explicitly states medieval fort-towns 'came up on the ruins of ancient towns,' meaning they typically built upon or reused earlier ancient-town sites, not entirely new, unconnected locations. Statements 1 and 2 are correct."})

